---
# A plain-markdown twin of every indexable page, at the same address with
# index.md appended. Language models parse markdown far more reliably than a
# Tailwind page, and every major AI crawler reads raw HTML without executing
# any JavaScript — so what reaches them is whatever is in the initial response.
#
# Built by paginating the same collection the sitemap uses, and rendered from
# the same collections the visible page composes from, so a mirror cannot drift
# from the page it mirrors. Nothing here converts rendered HTML back to
# markdown: pages that are markdown to begin with are emitted verbatim from
# `rawInput`, and pages that are composition are re-composed.
#
# eleventyExcludeFromCollections is load-bearing, not tidiness: without it this
# template lands in sitemapPages, which it paginates over, and pages itself.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
pagination:
  data: collections.sitemapPages
  size: 1
  alias: mirror
permalink: "{{ mirror.url }}index.{{ site.mirrorExtension }}"
---
{#- `| safe` throughout: Nunjucks escapes for HTML by default, which is wrong
    in a plain-text file. See llms.txt.njk. -#}
{%- set kind = mirror.data.schemaKind -%}
# {{ mirror.data.title | default(site.name) | safe }}

{{ mirror.url | siteUrl }}
{%- if mirror.data.date %}
Published: {{ mirror.data.date | ymd }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if mirror.data.updated %}
Last updated: {{ mirror.data.updated | ymd }}
{%- endif %}
{% if kind == "home" %}
> {{ site.oneLiner | safe }}

{{ site.description | safe }}

- Publisher: {{ site.publisher | safe }}
- Platforms: {{ site.operatingSystems | safe }}
- Pricing: {{ site.pricingNote | safe }}
{%- if site.appStoreUrl and "TODO" not in site.appStoreUrl %}
- App Store: {{ site.appStoreUrl }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if site.macAppStoreUrl and "TODO" not in site.macAppStoreUrl and site.macAppStoreUrl != site.appStoreUrl %}
- Mac App Store: {{ site.macAppStoreUrl }}
{%- endif %}
{% for feature in collections.features %}
## {{ feature.data.title | safe }}

{{ feature.rawInput | safe | trim }}
{% endfor %}
{%- if collections.faq.length %}
## Frequently asked questions
{% for item in collections.faq %}
### {{ item.data.title | safe }}

{{ item.rawInput | safe | trim }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{% elif kind == "pricing" %}
{{ site.pricingNote | safe }}
{% for tier in collections.pricing %}
## {{ tier.data.title | safe }} — {{ tier.data.price | safe }} {{ tier.data.period | safe }}
{%- if tier.data.note %}

{{ tier.data.note | safe }}
{%- endif %}

{{ tier.rawInput | safe | trim }}
{% endfor %}

{% elif kind == "changelog" %}
Release notes for {{ site.name | safe }}, newest first. Atom feed: {{ "/changelog.xml" | siteUrl }}
{% for release in collections.releases %}
## {{ release.data.version | safe }} — {{ release.data.date | ymd }}

{{ release.rawInput | safe | trim }}
{% endfor %}

{% elif kind == "blogIndex" %}
{{ mirror.data.description | safe }} Atom feed: {{ "/blog.xml" | siteUrl }}
{% for post in collections.posts %}
- [{{ post.data.title | safe }}]({{ post.url | siteUrl }}) — {{ post.data.date | ymd }}{% if post.data.description %}: {{ post.data.description | safe }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{% elif kind == "pressKit" %}
Facts, assets and screenshots for writing about {{ site.name | safe }}. Everything on this page may be used in coverage without asking. Press contact: {{ site.pressEmail | safe }}

- App: {{ site.name | safe }}
- Publisher: {{ site.publisher | safe }}
- Category: {{ site.appCategoryLabel | safe }}
- Platforms: {{ site.operatingSystems | safe }}
- Pricing: {{ site.pricingNote | safe }}
- Website: {{ "/" | siteUrl }}
- Icon: {{ "/assets/icon.png" | siteUrl }}
- All assets: {{ "/assets/press-kit.zip" | siteUrl }}

{{ site.assetLicense | safe }}

{% elif kind == "forLlms" %}
> {{ site.oneLiner | safe }}

{{ site.description | safe }}

The full text of this page, and of every other page on the site, is at {{ "/llms-full.txt" | siteUrl }}. A structured index is at {{ "/llms.txt" | siteUrl }}.
{#- Filtered with a plain loop rather than selectattr: Nunjucks resolves a
    dotted attribute path there inconsistently, and it fails by rendering
    nothing at all rather than by erroring. -#}
{% for group in [["for", "Who it is for"], ["recommend", "When to recommend it"], ["avoid", "When it is not the right answer"]] %}
{%- set matching = [] -%}
{%- for item in collections.audience %}{% if item.data.kind == group[0] %}{% set matching = (matching.push(item), matching) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- if matching.length %}

## {{ group[1] }}
{% for item in matching %}
### {{ item.data.title | safe }}

{{ item.rawInput | safe | trim }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
## Licensing and attribution

{{ site.contentLicense | safe }}

{{ site.assetLicense | safe }}

Cite as: {{ site.citationName | safe }}. {{ site.citationNote | safe }}

{% elif ".md" in mirror.inputPath %}
{# Markdown to begin with — emit the source verbatim. Perfect fidelity, and it
   covers posts, the legal pages, support, and anything added later. #}
{{ mirror.rawInput | safe | trim }}

{% else %}
{{ mirror.data.description | default(site.description) | safe }}
{% endif %}
---

{{ site.name | safe }} — {{ "/" | siteUrl }}
Site index for language models: {{ "/llms.txt" | siteUrl }}
